-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only. Search first with mem_search({query, mode: \"auto\", project}) to avoid duplicate or conflicting notes. For guided research, use mode: \"guided\" and follow each returned continuation through mem-search steps 1, 2, and 3. A hosted read-only connector may expose searches without write tools; do not call a missing write tool.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: call mem_search directly when its result is needed."}
